+FIXED
+
+# cluster ci-b303065974a069ae — macOS arm64 Qt 5 build failure in RowTableViewTest
+
+**Verdict: REAL (test-only portability defect, product code correct).** On the pinned train commit
+`31f559ab479dcd1b822545aae477222f58f32c0d` the hosted `macos-arm64` build stops at 66 % because
+`tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp` calls `QAbstractItemView::itemDelegateForIndex()`, which Qt 5 does not
+declare. The CI job uses Homebrew `qt@5` (`/opt/homebrew/opt/qt@5/lib/QtTest.framework` in the evidence log), so
+the test source — not `lmms::gui::RowTableView` — is the failing component.
+
+The product class is healthy: `include/RowTableView.h:37` derives from `QTableView`, and
+`src/gui/RowTableView.cpp:121` installs the row delegate with `setItemDelegate(m_rowDelegate)`, the view-level
+default that covers every index including rows inserted after `setModel()`. No production change is warranted.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Failure in the supplied CI log: `RowTableViewTest.cpp:54:59: error: no member named 'itemDelegateForIndex' in
+  'lmms::gui::RowTableView'` and the same at `:57`; `make: *** [all] Error 2`.
+- Original test calls were `tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:54` and `:57` (before this fix).
+- Qt 5.15.13 declares only `QAbstractItemDelegate *itemDelegate(const QModelIndex &index) const;` —
+  `/home/kruzzzzy/.local/opt/qt5/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/qt5/QtWidgets/qabstractitemview.h:226`.
+- Qt 6 declares `virtual QAbstractItemDelegate *itemDelegateForIndex(const QModelIndex &index) const;` and
+  forwards the deprecated Qt 6 `itemDelegate(index)` to it —
+  `/usr/include/qt6/QtWidgets/qabstractitemview.h:204-208`.
+- The class itself adds no such member (`include/RowTableView.h:37-52`).
+- The same repair exists on sibling branches (`2eb481c6fd`, `a8ad91c1a0`, `9ccb6cc841`), but it is **not** in this
+  branch's history: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 2eb481c6fd HEAD` returned `EXIT=1`. The test at HEAD is the
+  broken version, so this is not ALREADY-FIXED here.
+- Fix: `tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:32-39` adds a `QT_VERSION`-guarded `rowDelegate()` helper
+  (`itemDelegateForIndex` on Qt 6, `itemDelegate(index)` on Qt 5), used at `:64` and `:67`. Only the test source
+  changed: no product code, no project data, no audio path, no command or undo step.
+
