+
+The 4b patch reverses the only changed hunk. Because the defect is a Qt-6-only API call in the test source, the
+test-only guard *is* the fix: there is no product hunk to reverse, and adding a Qt-6 compatibility method to
+`RowTableView` just to satisfy a test would grow public API for no user-visible behaviour.
+
+## Self-check
+
+- **Regression fails with the fix reverted and passes restored.** Qt 5.15 harness: reverted build **EXIT=1** with
+  the two exact CI errors; restored build **EXIT=0** and test **EXIT=0** (6/6 pass). The local Qt 6 build passes
+  both ways because Qt 6 has the method; the platform-build leg is the meaningful RED/GREEN.
+- **Deterministic.** Compile-time API check plus direct model/view calls. No wall-clock timing, sleeps, threads,
+  races or randomness; no timestamps needed.
+- **Cause and completeness.** Searched the whole tree for `itemDelegateForIndex`: only this test used it. The
+  helper covers both Qt 5 and Qt 6 builds and both original call sites. `RowTableView` has no override or sibling
+  path that needs changing; the product's `setItemDelegate` call is already the correct view-level installation.
+- **No collateral damage.** No production code, save format, project loader, command registry, undo or audio code
+  changed. Old projects and saved data are untouched. No new limit or check was added.
+- **Realtime / undo / commands.** The diff is a test-only source file; nothing runs on the audio thread, and no
+  command, undo step or reversibility class changed.
+- **Old projects and round-trip.** Not applicable: no serialization, project model or product behaviour changed.
+- **GUI path.** The test drives the real `RowTableView` widget with a real `QStandardItemModel`; it uses the same
+  delegate query the view uses and asserts an inserted row inherits the row delegate.
+- **Portability.** The change removes a Qt-6-only call from test source behind `QT_VERSION`; Qt 5.15 and Qt 6 both
+  compile it. No `windows.h`, no `std::filesystem`, no new platform assumption.
+
+Files committed: `tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp` and this report.
